<!-- EDGE CASES & BOUNDARIES — what the code handles (and doesn't) -->
<h2 id="edge-cases">&#9888;&#65039; Edge Cases &amp; Boundaries</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Edge Case</th><th>What Happens</th><th>Where in Code</th><th>Risk Level</th></tr>
<tr><td>Empty graph (no nodes)</td><td>execute() returns empty outputs, empty history</td><td>Canvas.execute()</td><td>&#128994; Low — not an error, just a no-op</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Cyclic dependencies</td><td>topological_sort() fails; canvas.load() raises ValidationError</td><td>Canvas.load()</td><td>&#128308; High — prevents any execution</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Variable not found (e.g., undefined_node@output)</td><td>get_variable_value() returns None; component behavior depends on parameter nullable config</td><td>Canvas.execute()</td><td>&#128308; High — may cause downstream component failure</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Tool not registered</td><td>Agent.run() calls registry.get_tool(name); KeyError raised; caught and handled via retry/fallback</td><td>Component.run()</td><td>&#128308; High — workflow branch fails unless exception_goto or exception_default_value configured</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Iteration with 0 items</td><td>Iteration.run() loop doesn't execute sub-DAG; returns empty results list</td><td>Iteration.run()</td><td>&#128994; Low — valid behavior; batch size can be 0</td></tr>
  <tr><td>LLM timeout during chat</td><td>Exception caught in LLM.run(); retry logic kicks in (exponential backoff); if all retries fail, exception_default_value used</td><td>LLM.run()</td><td>&#128308; High — affects workflow success; requires fallback strategy</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Concurrent access</td><td>How it's handled</td><td>function_name:line</td><td>&#128308; High</td></tr>
  <!-- Add 3-6 rows covering known edge cases -->
</table>

